4. DEVELOPMENT PHILOSOPHY
The developer must follow these principles:
DO
●   Reuse good existing components where technically appropriate.
●   Preserve useful existing content.
●   Improve existing functionality rather than unnecessarily replacing it.
●   Build reusable components.
●   Build CMS-driven content.
●   Build relational content architecture.
●   Build AI as a platform layer.
●   Build monetization into the architecture.
●   Test every feature end-to-end.
●   Optimize for mobile, SEO, performance and security.
DO NOT
●   Build a superficial chatbot and call the website AI-powered.
●   Hard-code content that should be CMS-controlled.
●   Create separate disconnected systems.
●   Use fake testimonials.
●   Use fake metrics.
●   Use fake advertising results.
●   Fabricate case-study results.
●   Leave unfinished public features.
●   Expose API keys.
●   Create unnecessary technical debt.
The original specification explicitly requires inspection of the existing website/codebase before rebuilding and requires a working production-ready platform rather than mockups.
